menu "Michi Music Stream Pairing"

    comment "Receiver-button pairing (MS-06): the window opens ONLY from the physical button; tokens are stored as SHA-256 digests (never plaintext). PIN attempts and rate limits are fixed contract constants in michi_pairing.h."

    config MICHI_PAIRING_WINDOW_SECONDS
        int "Pairing window duration (s)"
        default 120
        range 5 3600
        help
          How long a pairing window (opened by the physical button)
          stays open before it expires and closes itself (one-shot
          esp_timer -> MICHI_EVENT_PAIRING_WINDOW_CLOSED, PAIRING -> IDLE
          in the FSM). Monotonic clock. A reboot always closes it (the
          window is not persisted); re-opening replaces the previous
          window and drops pending pairing sessions. The default is 5 s:
          the physical button is the only window opener (no network-visible
          trigger), so a short window is a safe default - a press not
          followed by a controller pairing expires quickly instead of
          leaving the device discoverable for minutes.

    config MICHI_PAIRING_MAX_CONTROLLERS
        int "Maximum paired controllers"
        default 8
        range 1 16
        help
          Maximum registry entries persisted in the NVS "michi_pairing"
          namespace (one versioned blob). Reaching the limit rejects new
          confirmations until a controller is revoked.

endmenu
